          "create_time": 1793050065.114,
          "update_time": 1793050073.869,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Created the [current summary](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/02_heat_flow_rh_applications/summary/CURRENT_SUMMARY.md) in a new `summary` folder. It preserves all eight bound targets from the brainstorm, keeps the alternatives open, and prioritizes your Rodgers–Tao question. I also saved a [detailed analysis](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-5/02_heat_flow_rh_applications/notes/02_RODGERS_TAO_POSITIVE_THRESHOLD_20261026.md) and refreshed the chat history.\n\n**Assuming \\(\\Lambda>0\\) is a legitimate contradiction strategy—it would prove RH if successful.** The difficulty is that Rodgers–Tao’s contradiction depends on reaching the particular slice \\(t=0\\).\n\nUnder \\(\\Lambda<0\\), the zeros have been real and repelling one another for a positive duration **before reaching the zeta zeros at time zero**. Their argument forces excessively regular spacing there, contradicting known zeta spacing results. [Rodgers–Tao, §9](https://arxiv.org/html/1801.05914v5)\n\nUnder \\(\\Lambda>0\\), the all-real interval begins **after** time zero. Relaxation then produces regular spacing at positive times—which is compatible with the assumption. Indeed, sufficiently high zeros already have this behavior at every fixed positive time, without assuming RH. Shifting the time origin does not restore the missing zeta spacing information. [Polymath, Theorem 1.5](https://arxiv.org/html/1904.12438v2)\n\nThe elementary heat solution\n\\[\nF(t,z)=z^2-2(t-T)\n\\]\nshows the local issue: for any \\(T>0\\), its zeros are nonreal before \\(T\\), double at \\(T\\), and real and simple afterward. Forward repulsion permits an earlier collision.\n\n**The promising adaptation is therefore to investigate that collision.** A positive Newman threshold would force a multiple zero at some finite height. Could the new bounds prevent the local interaction energy from concentrating there, or certify a margin excluding simultaneous \\(H=H_z=0\\)? I recorded both as aspirational targets. They could guide the intermediate estimates, while a complete bound on a fixed positive-time region could first yield an incremental improvement in the Newman upper bound."
            ]
          },
